# Sasha Ivliskova, the bride in webs (prop cat_sasha_bier, crypt 20 in the Lesser Vaults). Speaking to her wakes her; the
# only way to stop it is not to speak. She asks if her love has come, and whatever the answer, she is hungry.

~ bier
narrate examine:cat_sasha_bier
if flag.cat_sasha_slain
-> END
endif
* Lean close to the shroud and speak her name. -> wake
* Step back from the bier and leave her be. -> END

~ wake
sasha_ivliskova: Is that your lantern at the gate, my heart? Have you come down at last to fetch me home?
-> menu

~ menu
* Who is it you are waiting for? -> who
* No one is coming for you. -> no
* Ease the stone lid back into place. -> leave

~ who
sasha_ivliskova: My husband, Ivan Ivliskovich. His greyhounds took the winter riband three years running, and he promised we should have a house by the river when the snow melted.
-> menu

~ no
sasha_ivliskova: You lie with a warm throat. If Ivan is not behind you, then you have only brought me supper.
combat cat_sasha

~ leave
Narrator: You lower the stone into its groove and the grey webs settle back across her face. From the dark beneath comes a small breath of relief, and one dry sob.
-> END
